20	2	\N	\N	Contact us	contact-us	0	2016-07-04 23:11:34.643322	2016-07-10 22:36:30.15026	GeneralContent	\N	published	1b97dcab-9355-41bf-abe4-aeceeb96e6c1	\N	\N	{"content_body": "**You can contact us in a number of ways.**\\r\\n\\r\\n## Email  \\r\\n\\r\\n#### Copyright\\r\\n[copyright@communications.gov.au](mailto:copyright@communications.gov.au)\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Media enquiries\\r\\n[media@communications.gov.au](mailto:media@communications.gov.au)\\r\\n\\r\\n## Phone\\r\\n[02 6271 1000](tel:+61262711000)  \\r\\nFree call: [1800 254 649](tel:1800254649)  \\r\\n9am – 5pm AEDST  \\r\\nMonday to Friday excluding ACT public holidays  \\r\\n\\r\\nIf you have a hearing or speech impairment, use the [National Relay Service](http://relayservice.gov.au/) to access any of our listed phone numbers.  \\r\\nTelephone: [1300 555 727](tel:1300555727)\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Media enquiries\\r\\n\\r\\n[02 6271 1777](tel:+61262711777)\\r\\n9am – 5pm AEDST<br>\\r\\nMonday to Friday excluding ACT public holidays\\r\\n\\r\\n## Locations and opening hours\\r\\n\\r\\n38 Sydney Avenue  \\r\\nForrest ACT 2608  \\r\\n9am – 5pm AEDST  \\r\\nMonday to Friday excluding ACT public holidays  \\r\\n\\r\\n## Post\\r\\n\\r\\nDepartment of Communications and the Arts  \\r\\nGPO Box 2154  \\r\\nCanberra ACT 2601  \\r\\nAustralia\\r\\n\\r\\n## Social media\\r\\n\\r\\nLinkedin: [Department of Communications and the Arts](https://www.linkedin.com/company/commsau)  \\r\\nTwitter: [@CommsAu](https://twitter.com/CommsAu)  \\r\\nYoutube: [Department of Communications and the Arts](https://www.youtube.com/user/DeptCommsAu)  \\r\\n\\r\\n#### Arts\\r\\n\\r\\nTwitter: [@ArtsCultureGov](https://twitter.com/ArtsCultureGov)  \\r\\n\\r\\n## How we handle enquiries\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [Client Service Charter](javascript:void(0))  \\r\\nWe aim to provide you with a high level of service.  \\r\\n\\r\\n#### [Complaints Handling Policy](javascript:void(0))  \\r\\nHow to complain about us and have your concerns addressed.\\r\\n    \\r\\n#### [Privacy Policy](javascript:void(0))  \\r\\nHow we handle personal and sensitive information.  \\r\\n\\r\\n#### [Reporting Fraud Policy](javascript:void(0))  \\r\\nYou are strongly encouraged to report any suspected fraud incidents against us.  \\r\\n    \\r\\n#### [Public Interest Disclosure](javascript:void(0))  \\r\\nHow to report serious wrongdoing in the Commonwealth public sector.  \\r\\n\\r\\n#### [Freedom of information (FOI) requests](javascript:void(0))  \\r\\nLearn more about our FOI obligations and how to make a request.  "}
7	2	\N	\N	Our role	our-role	0	2016-07-01 04:15:00.082835	2016-07-10 22:36:34.332229	GeneralContent	\N	published	97cad92d-7e84-4ad5-92b6-3acdae0216cc	\N	\N	{"content_body": "**Through our analysis, advice and programs we aim to make the arts and communications sectors better for everyone.**\\r\\n\\r\\nWe help the communications sector stay competitive and innovative by providing advice, delivering programs and conducting research.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe also manage programs that encourage artists, support Australia's cultural heritage and help everyone experience arts and culture.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Internet\\r\\n\\r\\nProviding access to high-quality, reliable and affordable internet services.\\r\\n\\r\\n* [Internet speeds](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n* [Internet safety](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Television\\r\\n\\r\\nRegulating the TV industry and its services.\\r\\n\\r\\n* [Television reception](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n* [Television content rules](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Phone\\r\\n\\r\\nEnsuring everyone has reasonable access to reliable phone services.\\r\\n\\r\\n* [Mobile phone black spots](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n* [Accessible phone services](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Radio\\r\\n\\r\\nGiving everyone access to radio and assisting in the roll-out of digital radio.\\r\\n\\r\\n* [Digital radio](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n* [Content classification](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Post\\r\\n\\r\\nAdvising the Australian Government on how the postal industry can best serve the public.\\r\\n\\r\\n* [Posting in Australia and overseas](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Spectrum\\r\\n\\r\\nEnsuring the electromagnetic spectrum can be used with current electronic devices.\\r\\n\\r\\n* [Spectrum licences](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n* [Emergency services](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n* [Digital dividend spectrum](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Copyright\\r\\n\\r\\nProviding legal protection for people who express ideas and information in certain forms.\\r\\n\\r\\n* [Copyright](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n* [Intellectual property (IP)](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Classification\\r\\n\\r\\nHelping the Classification Board to make decisions about the classification of films, television, books and music.\\r\\n\\r\\n* [The classification code](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Arts\\r\\n\\r\\nEncouraging excellence in art, support for cultural heritage and public access to arts and culture.\\r\\n\\r\\n* [Prime Minister's Literary Awards](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n* [Lending rights](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n* [Arts funding](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## Related government agencies\\r\\n\\r\\nWe work closely with the agencies that provide you with communication and arts services.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [Australia Council for the Arts](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Australian Government's arts funding and advisory body.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [Australia Post](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nProviding reliable and affordable postal, retail, financial and travel services.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [Australian Broadcasting corporation (ABC)](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nAustralia’s public broadcaster, including national and local television and radio programs.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [Australian Communications and Media Authority (ACMA)](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nResponsible for the regulation of broadcasting, the internet, radiocommunications and telecommunications.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [Australian Film Television and Radio School (AFTRS)](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nThe leading institution for the education and training of creative talent.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [Australian National Maritime Museum](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nAustralia’s national centre for maritime collections, exhibitions, research and archaeology.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [Bundanon Trust](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nSupporting arts practice and engagement through education, exhibition and performance programs.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [Australia Business Arts Foundation (operating as Creative Partnerships Australia)](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nBringing artists, donors, businesses and arts organisations together to promote a more sustainable and vibrant arts sector.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [The Museum of Australian Democracy](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nHelping people to understand Australia’s social and political history by interpreting the past and present and exploring the future.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [National Film and Sound Archive](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nThe nation’s living archive – collecting, preserving and sharing our rich audiovisual heritage.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [National Gallery of Australia (NGA)](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nAustralia's national cultural institution for the visual arts.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [National Library of Australia (NLA)](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nEnsuring that important documentary resources are collected, preserved and made accessible to the public.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [National Museum of Australia](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nA social history museum exploring the land, nation and people of Australia.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [National Portrait Gallery Australia (NPGA)](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nThe national collection of portraits of Australians reflects the breadth and energy of Australian culture and endeavour.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [NBN Co Limited](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nDelivering Australia’s first national, open access broadband network to all Australians.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [Office of the Children’s e-Safety Co](javascript:void(0))mmissioner\\r\\n\\r\\nCommitted to helping young people have safe, positive experiences online.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [Screen Australia](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nFunding the production of everything from feature films to documentaries, television drama, children’s programs and online web series.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### [Special broadcasting service (SBS)](javascript:void(0))\\r\\n\\r\\nAustralia’s multicultural and multilingual broadcaster."}
18	2	\N	\N	Performance reports	performance-reports	0	2016-07-04 23:06:44.60079	2016-07-10 22:36:38.79885	GeneralContent	\N	published	c2046dcf-0a2e-4efa-8b52-3ba1246b9e49	\N	\N	{"content_body": "Test"}
16	2	\N	\N	Careers	careers	0	2016-07-04 23:03:24.763132	2016-07-10 22:36:44.035641	GeneralContent	\N	published	a183986f-5191-46d4-8cc8-d8bf30ab055b	\N	\N	{"content_body": "**Learn more about our workplace culture and the many benefits of working here.**\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## Current job opportunities\\r\\n\\r\\n<a class=\\"see-more\\" href=\\"https://communications.nga.net.au\\">Visit our Jobs page</a>\\r\\n\\r\\n## What we work on\\r\\n\\r\\nWe promote an innovative and competitive communications sector by undertaking analysis, providing advice and delivering programs.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe also manage programs that encourage excellence in art, support for cultural heritage and public access to arts and culture.\\r\\n\\r\\nTo find out more, see [Our responsibilities](/comms-arts-agency/what-we-do-comms.html).\\r\\n\\r\\n## The benefits of working here\\r\\n\\r\\n* a good salary with opportunities to develop your career in policy areas that affect most Australians\\r\\n* ongoing training and development opportunities\\r\\n* access to study assistance\\r\\n* access to new technology to support flexible work arrangements\\r\\n* flexible working hours\\r\\n* generous leave conditions\\r\\n* an attractive superannuation scheme\\r\\n* access to mentoring programs\\r\\n* a staff job rotation program and portfolio agency secondment program\\r\\n* in-house capability development programs\\r\\n* an excellent wellbeing program and social club.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Our workplace culture\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Wellbeing program\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Wellbeing Program includes seminars and activities that focus on the social, mental and physical health of employees. It includes free influenza vaccinations, a carer's room, health seminars, quit smoking assistance, annual health checks, cooking demonstrations and physical activities such as lunchtime walking groups.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Employee Assistance Program\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Employee Assistance Program is a confidential, professional short-term counselling service. All our staff can access the program as a face-to-face service during work hours (by appointment) and by telephone during or outside of work hours. It is a free service for our employees and their immediate families.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Smoke-free workplace\\r\\n\\r\\nAs an employer, we have a duty of care to protect our staff from passive smoking while they are working. We provide financial assistance to staff and members of their immediate families who want to quit smoking. There are designated smoking areas.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Learning and development\\r\\n\\r\\nOur employees have opportunities for learning and development throughout their careers including:  \\r\\n\\r\\n* an induction program for new employees\\r\\n* a core training program with short courses for business skills and knowledge\\r\\n* development programs to build management and leadership skills\\r\\n* an internal rotation program to help our employees broaden their skills and knowledge.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Study assistance\\r\\n\\r\\nStudybank is our study assistance program. It helps our employees develop their work-related skills through access to:  \\r\\n\\r\\n* up to 75 hours paid leave per semester for study\\r\\n* financial assistance of up to $5000 per calendar year as per the Enterprise Agreement.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Vacation care\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Vacation Childcare Subsidisation Program reimburses up to $15.45 a day (the maximum per family) for children aged between five and 12 years. To qualify for the allowance, children must attend a registered child care service or a certified vacation care facility during the school holidays.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Carers’ room\\r\\n\\r\\nOur carers’ room is available for staff who need to take care of immediate family members in an emergency. It gives people an alternative to using leave. Conditions of use apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Eldercare\\r\\n\\r\\nOur eldercare information kit contains information on eldercare issues and how to deal with them. The kit is a national resource that has information on all states and territories.\\r\\n\\r\\n#### Employment agreement\\r\\n\\r\\nFor details, read our [Enterprise agreement](javascript:void(0))."}
